commit 1480c0543832ec26c032866e8644c0b0f5178e70
Author:     Henry Cikanek <cikanekhenry@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: 2025-11-03
Commit:     GitHub <noreply@github.com>
CommitDate: 2025-11-04

    feat(chat): Add task generation endpoint [EVO-2258]
    
    * feat(chat-stream): Add SSE endpoint for chat (proxy to ms) [EVO-2258]
    
    * feat(task-mode): Add task generation endpoint [EVO-2258]
    
    * feat(chat): Add task generation endpoint [EVO-2258]
    
    Add new /chat/tasks endpoint for non-streaming task generation mode:
    
    - Add chatTasks() service method to proxy requests to microservice
    - Add chatTasksController to handle task generation requests
    - Implement conversation persistence with proper message-task association
    - Add FOLLOW_UP_SUGGESTIONS cleanup for consistent response formatting
    - Add POST /api/v1/ai/chat/tasks route with authentication
    
    The new endpoint mirrors the streaming chat endpoint's user context
    gathering and conversation saving logic, ensuring tasks are properly
    associated with the messages that generated them. This supports the
    frontend's task mode feature while maintaining conversation history.
    
    Technical notes:
    - Tasks are saved within message objects (msg.tasks) for proper
      multi-turn conversation support
    - Microservice returns tasks both at top level (backward compatibility)
      and within messages (proper association)
    - Save logic matches existing /chat endpoint for consistency
    
    * feat(task): Prevent duplicate AI task creation with unique IDs
    
    - Add aiGeneratedTaskId field to Task model with unique compound index (user + aiGeneratedTaskId)
    - Generate UUID for each AI-generated task in chatTasksController and include in conversation storage
    - Implement duplicate prevention in createTask service - return existing task if aiGeneratedTaskId matches
    - Fix bug where aiGeneratedTaskId wasn't being returned to frontend in chat/tasks API response
    - Add debug logging to track task creation flow and duplicate detection
    
    This prevents duplicate tasks when users accept the same AI-generated tasks multiple times.
    The backend now generates unique IDs for AI tasks and enforces idempotency at both application and database levels.

