    feat(calendar): Migrate sync from cron to webhook push [EVO-2255] (#473)
    
    * feat(calendar): Migrate sync from cron to webhook push [EVO-2255]
    
    Refactor Google Calendar synchronization from polling-based cron jobs to event-driven webhook push notifications for real-time updates
    
    Key Changes:
    - Add webhookService for Google Calendar push notifications
    - Add WebhookRenewalScheduler to manage webhook lifecycle (7-day TTL)
    - Add calendarWebhook controller for handling push notifications
    - Remove calendarSyncCronService (legacy cron-based sync)
    - Update CalendarSyncScheduler to handle manual syncs and failures
    - Enhance logging with structured metadata and context
    - Update calendar settings service with webhook management
    - Add webhook routes and endpoints
    
    Benefits:
    - Real-time calendar sync instead of periodic polling
    - Reduced API quota usage (no more frequent polling)
    - Better scalability and performance
    - Automatic webhook renewal before expiration
    
    Technical Details:
    - Webhook channels expire after 7 days and auto-renew
    - Fallback to manual sync for edge cases
    - Comprehensive error handling and logging
    - Google Calendar API v3 push notifications
    
    JIRA: EVO-2255
    
    * refactor(webhooks): Remove manual force-refresh API endpoint
    
    JIRA: EVO-2255
    
    * feat(webhooks): Add environment-based force renewal on startup
    
    Force renew all webhooks on dev/development startup to ensure correct BASE_URL
    when dev and local environments share the same database. Production only sets
    up missing webhooks without force renewal for efficiency.
    
    JIRA: EVO-2255
    
    * refactor(webhooks): Deduplicate code and centralize webhook logic
    
    - Create reusable setupWebhookForCalendar() to eliminate duplicated setup logic
    - Add setupWebhooksForNewCalendars() for immediate webhook setup on calendar link
    - Add stopWebhooksForRemovedCalendars() for calendar deselection handling
    - Create stopWebhooksForCalendars() helper to deduplicate webhook stopping logic
    - Add cleanupWebhookMetadata() utility for API failure cases
    - Centralize ALL webhook logic in webhookService.js (separation of concerns)
    - Remove unused setupWebhooksForUser() function (dead code)
    - Update WebhookRenewalScheduler to use shared setupWebhookForCalendar()
    - Add immediate webhook setup on calendar link (no cron delay)
    - Add webhook cleanup when calendars removed from selection
    - Add webhook cleanup on complete calendar unlink
    
    Benefits:
    - 254 lines of duplicated code eliminated
    - Webhooks set up immediately on link (real-time sync within seconds)
    - All webhook logic properly isolated in webhookService
    - Single source of truth for webhook operations
    - OAuth service simplified and focused on OAuth flow only
    - Improved testability and maintainability
    
    JIRA: EVO-2255
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Umesh Shrestha <stha.ums@gmail.com>

