    feat(scheduler): Add task auto-sched cron with service auth [EVO-2102]
    
    * fix(calendar): Resolve scheduling and task-event deletion [EVO-2102]
    
    * fix(work-time-prefs): Pass work-day preferences correctly [EVO-2102]
    
    * fix(scheduler): Prevent dup times in rapid task creation [EVO-2102]
    
    - Query events from start of day to detect recently scheduled tasks
    - Remove timezone-misinterpreting sanitization for microservice responses
    - Make task creation synchronous with scheduling to enforce ordering
    
    * feat(scheduler): Add task auto-sched cron with service auth [EVO-2102]
    
    - Create TaskAutoScheduler cron service that runs daily at 6 AM UTC
    - Auto-schedule tasks with HIGH priority or deadlines within 3 days
    - Implement service-to-service authentication using static token
    - Use queue mechanism to prevent concurrency conflicts during scheduling
    - Add comprehensive logging for monitoring and debugging
    - Skip tasks that already have auto-scheduled events
    - Handle errors gracefully per user/task without failing entire job
    - Update cron system documentation with new scheduler details
    
    BREAKING CHANGE: Requires SERVICE_AUTH_TOKEN environment variable in both
    backend and microservice for internal API communication
    
    Backend changes:
    - services/cron/TaskAutoScheduler.js: New cron job implementation
    - services/cron/index.js: Register TaskAutoScheduler in cron system
    - services/cron/README.md: Document new auto-scheduler job
    - services/cron/TASK_AUTO_SCHEDULER.md: Detailed implementation guide
    
    The service token format is 'Bearer service:{token}' to distinguish
    from user JWTs. This enables proper authentication for automated
    internal operations while maintaining security.
    
    * fix(scheduler): Skip users with smart calendar disabled [EVO-2102]
    
    - Add smartCalendarEnabled check in TaskAutoScheduler
    - Fetch calendar settings before processing user tasks
    - Skip auto-scheduling for users who haven't enabled smart calendar
    - Add debug logging when skipping disabled users
    - Prevent unwanted auto-scheduling for users who opted out
    
    This prevents the cron job from processing tasks for users who have not
    enabled the smart calendar feature, saving resources and respecting user
    preferences.

