commit d71f3da65297e80a6d03c813818b989338d5762f
Author:     Umesh Shrestha <34161121+stha-ums@users.noreply.github.com>
AuthorDate: 2025-08-25
Commit:     GitHub <noreply@github.com>
CommitDate: 2025-08-25

    EV0-1526; calender settings api (#328)
    
    * EV0-1526; calender settings api
    
    * Smart Calendar backend: add workItems→eventProposals flow, return suggestedEvents and ready-to-post eventPayloads; normalize prefs (weekday segments + timezone). Wire FastAPI calendar base, add Zod validation, and Swagger docs for analyze, schedule, conflicts, optimize. Provide smoke script and keep smart-calendar endpoints read-only (FE accepts via existing /events).
    
    * Began building the scaffolding for scheduled tasks to event flow. That is to say the ability for the backend to place tasks that have a scheduled date into a prospective time slot within the calendar. This will be only as proposed events, leveraging functionality already built within the smart calendar feature.
    
    * Continued progress on the development of the task to event pipeline
    
    * feat: implement task-to-event auto-scheduling with microservice integration
    
    - Fix auth header passing through event emission system
    - Integrate smart-schedule microservice with proper field mapping (work_items vs tasks)
    - Add fallback to basic scheduling when microservice returns no proposals
    - Support eligibility criteria: HIGH priority OR due within 3 days
    - Add timezone sanitization for unreasonable scheduling times
    
    * Standardize scheduler payload: replace preferredDate with deadline
    Background auto-scheduler (services/taskEventSchedulerService.js)
    Work item shape now: { id, title, durationMins, deadline }
    deadline is sourced from task.endDate (frontend “Due Date”)
    Removed preferredDate from payload
    Smart calendar controller (controllers/smartCalendar/index.js)
    convertTasksToWorkItems now emits deadline instead of preferredDate
    Keeps both duration_mins and durationMins for compatibility
    No change to envelope keys (work_items vs tasks/workItems), dateRange, or existingEvents
    Rationale
    Aligns with domain terminology: “Due Date” → scheduling deadline
    Simplifies microservice input normalization; preferredDate deprecated
    
    * chore: ignore packages/server/globalConfig.json (local jest artifact)
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Henry Cikanek <cikanekhenry@gmail.com>

